> //
> // Emulated WH_JOURNALPLAYBACK support. Modern Windows (Vista+) blocks
> // journal hooks (SetWindowsHookEx returns NULL / ERROR_ACCESS_DENIED), so
> // when a 16-bit app installs WH_JOURNALPLAYBACK we keep the hook WOW-side
> // (see wuhook.c) and drive it ourselves from the message pump. This holds
> // the vaHookStateData[] index of the active emulated playback hook, or -1.
> // (Old Access runtimes -- MSARN200 -- script their startup form via journal
> // playback; without this the modal form never receives its input and hangs.)
> //
> INT gW10JournalHookIdx = -1;
